  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">A refrigerator can keep food cold for about 4 hours if the door stays closed. A full freezer can keep food frozen for about 48 hours. When food has been above 40°F for more than 2 hours, it should usually be discarded.</p></div>


  
