  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><h2 style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true"><span class="sqsrte-text-color--darkAccent"><strong>What Foods Can Usually Be Saved?</strong></span></h2><h3 style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Some foods are less likely to spoil quickly and may be safe to keep if they remain at room temperature or were stored properly.</h3><p class="isSelectedEnd" style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Examples include:</p><ul data-rte-list="default"><li><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Unopened canned foods</p></li><li><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Shelf-stable foods</p></li><li><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Uncut fruits and vegetables</p></li><li><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Bread and baked goods</p></li><li><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Peanut butter</p></li><li><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Condiments such as mustard, ketchup, and pickles</p></li></ul><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;" data-rte-preserve-empty="true">Always inspect food carefully and discard anything that may have been contaminated.</p></div>


  
